{"beat": 5, "name": "THE FIVE-CENT TABLE", "text": "In 1878, a travelling salesman told his employer, William Moore, about something he'd seen in Michigan: a counter where everything cost a nickel. Moore ordered $100 of goods for one from a wholesaler, Spelman Brothers. Woolworth set out the table. In his own telling, years later, he gave himself more of the credit: I persuaded my employers to create a five cent cash counter with me in charge of it. A correction you'll need, because the story is usually told the other way: Woolworth didn't invent the nickel counter. He ran one, watched what it did, and asked the bigger question. Not what a nickel table could sell. What a whole store could, if every price in it was a nickel.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "In", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.1}, {"word": "1878,", "start": 0.1, "end": 1.96}, {"word": "a", "start": 2.5, "end": 2.64}, {"word": "travelling", "start": 2.64, "end": 3.1}, {"word": "salesman", "start": 3.1, "end": 3.82}, {"word": "told", "start": 3.82, "end": 4.08}, {"word": "his", "start": 4.08, "end": 4.32}, {"word": "employer,", "start": 4.32, "end": 4.84}, {"word": "William", "start": 5.12, "end": 5.32}, {"word": "Moore,", "start": 5.32, "end": 5.74}, {"word": "about", "start": 6.28, "end": 6.48}, {"word": "something", "start": 6.48, "end": 6.88}, {"word": "he'd", "start": 6.88, "end": 7.22}, {"word": "seen", "start": 7.22, "end": 7.52}, {"word": "in", "start": 7.52, "end": 7.72}, {"word": "Michigan:", "start": 7.72, "end": 8.06}, {"word": "a", "start": 8.72, "end": 8.86}, {"word": "counter", "start": 8.86, "end": 9.16}, {"word": "where", "start": 9.16, "end": 9.5}, {"word": "everything", "start": 9.5, "end": 9.96}, {"word": "cost", "start": 9.96, "end": 10.42}, {"word": "a", "start": 10.42, "end": 10.64}, {"word": "nickel.", "start": 10.64, "end": 10.9}, {"word": "Moore", "start": 11.64, "end": 11.86}, {"word": "ordered", "start": 11.86, "end": 12.28}, {"word": "$100", "start": 12.28, "end": 13